9.5 Understanding Every State

🔴 NEW
Definition:

Thread object is created.
start() has not been called.

Thread t = new Thread();

State:
NEW

🔴 RUNNABLE

Definition:

start() has been called.
Thread is eligible to run.
Scheduler decides when it executes.

Example:
t.start();

State:
RUNNABLE
Interview Point: Java combines the Ready and Running states into a single state called RUNNABLE.

🔴 BLOCKED

Definition:
The thread is waiting to acquire a monitor lock.

Example:
synchronized(obj){

}

🔴 If another thread already owns the lock:
BLOCKED

🔴 WAITING

Definition:
The thread waits indefinitely until another thread wakes it.

Methods causing WAITING:

wait()
join()
LockSupport.park()

🔴 TIMED_WAITING

Definition:
The thread waits for a specified amount of time.

Methods:

Thread.sleep(1000);
thread.join(5000);
object.wait(3000);

🔴 TERMINATED

Definition:
Thread execution has finished.

Example:
public void run(){

}

Once run() completes:

TERMINATED
A terminated thread cannot be restarted.

